  "term": "dolichocephalic",
  "definition": "In historical usage, dolichocephalic means long-headed, referring to a skull or head whose width is relatively small compared with its front-to-back length. It is the opposite of brachycephalic and was described as having a cephalic index well below the usual range, typically under 75:100.",
